2026-11-06T07:56:37.1513600Z 
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1513920Z LLD and LLDB are now provided in separate formulae:
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1544170Z   brew install lld
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1544510Z   brew install lldb
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1544690Z 
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1545080Z Z3 solver support will be removed in LLVM 24 as it is unsupported upstream,
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1553080Z see https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/205370
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1553400Z 
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1553730Z Using `clang`, `clang++`, etc., requires a CLT installation at `/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools`.
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1596690Z If you don't want to install the CLT, you can write appropriate configuration files pointing to your
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1597580Z SDK at ~/.config/clang.
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1597780Z 
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1598020Z To use the bundled libunwind please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1598450Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1598770Z 
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1598970Z To use the bundled libc++ please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1600100Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/c++ -L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1600730Z Features newer than system libc++ will require the following define to enable
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1601250Z (support for this may be removed in a future major LLVM release):
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1601680Z   CPPFLAGS="-D_LIBCPP_DISABLE_AVAILABILITY"
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1601870Z 
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1602270Z NOTE: You probably want to use the libunwind and libc++ provided by macOS unless you know what you're doing.
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1602660Z 
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1602880Z llvm is keg-only, which means it was not symlinked into /opt/homebrew,
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1603460Z because macOS already provides this software and installing another version in
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1603940Z parallel can cause all kinds of trouble.
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1604140Z 
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1604330Z If you need to have llvm first in your PATH, run:
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1604840Z   printf '%s\n' export\ PATH\=/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/bin:\$PATH >> /Users/runner/.bash_profile
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1605290Z 
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1605460Z For compilers to find llvm you may need to set:
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1606540Z   export LDFLAGS=-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1606930Z   export CPPFLAGS=-I/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/include
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1607210Z 
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1607380Z For cmake to find llvm you may need to set:
2026-11-06T07:56:37.1607800Z   export CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm
